{
  "_readme": "ZCode's app-server wire vocabulary, for the tables BOTH the Go provider and the TS renderer plugin read. ZCode speaks line-delimited JSON with no `jsonrpc` field, so the envelope's `type` and the payload's `kind` ARE the dispatch keys on both sides -- a one-character drift between the two copies silently stops rendering a row rather than failing a build. Only the tables that are genuinely duplicated live here. The Go-only vocabulary (client->server methods, error codes, reply field names, input sources, task kinds, scopes) and the frontend-only `display.kind` stay in their own file, per the contracts rule's one-side-only exemption. LeapMux does not own these values -- Z.ai does -- so a change here follows the app-server, it does not lead it.",
